  I'm guessing you don't appreciate the joys of multishot missiles.
Multishot missiles can fire more than one missile per throw (under the
right circumstances).  Daggers are multishot at Skilled or Expert.
Knives are never multishot.  (Don't ask me why.  It's the DevTeam wot
dunnit.)


  Expert thrown daggers essentially:
   - #twoweaponing, 
   - out to range Str/2, 
   - can wear a shield.  
   - can wield whatever weapon you like.
   - Use the stronger single-weapon skill table.

  That means:
   - double base damage.
   - double enchantment damage. 
   - double skill bonus damage.
   - double strength damage bonus.
   - double ring of increase damage. 
   - double blessed damage vs unholy monsters.

  Healers only get 1.5x, but that's still very nice.  


  The alternative is getting a lot of blessed poisoned enchanted darts
while carrying a non-cursed luckstone with high luck. (So the darts
don't disappear.)

  Darts weigh one-tenth as much as daggers, but will be gone after two
hits without multiple preparations that early characters have little
chance of accomplishing.

  Healers can get to Expert with darts and average 2 per fling.
Downside is that costs 6 skill slots.  Healers are already in skill slot
jail trying to find an early weapon, saving 6 skill slots for the Staff
of Aesculapius, and (hopefully) spending 3 skill slots for throwing
multi-shot daggers.




